### Dry Hire vs. Full Service AV Hire

"Dry hire" means equipment only, no technician, no setup help. That is not how we operate. Every package, from the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) up, is delivered, installed and tested by our crew, and collected again after your event. On the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), a dedicated technician also stays on site for the hours that matter, so a wireless mic dropping out mid speech is our problem to fix, not yours. If you searched for "AV hire near me" hoping to avoid setting up gear yourself, that is exactly what full service hire is for.

Our equipment also holds up outdoors: on beach ceremonies, villa terraces and rooftop events, our sound and lighting rigs are set up to handle the venue, weather permitting. For outdoor specific setup guidance, see [Audio Visual Rental for Outdoor Events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-outdoor-events/).

